    "whatWasObserved": "all three BLOCKED_BY_POLICY fetch observations produced by this window carry resolved_ip_family IPV6 and resolved_ip_is_public false, with no HTTP status. Two of them were the only request their run made",
    "corpusWideCount": "the whole database holds exactly six BLOCKED_BY_POLICY rows, all IPV6 and all non-public: three at about 14:5x UTC on 2026-09-25, which are the refusals that created the slot-51 and slot-54 obligations, and the three from this window at about 21:5x UTC on the same day",
    "theMechanism": "src/orgunits/web/address.ts refuses 64:ff9b::/96 as relay_or_translation, which is correct: a NAT64 prefix is not a public address. Under DNS64 an IPv4-only host resolves ONLY into that prefix, so the whole host is refused before DNS-to-socket",
    "whyThisIsNotAPolicyDefect": "the address rule is a network-scope guard and rule 18 forbids weakening it. Refusing a translation prefix is the gateway behaving as designed",
    "whyItIsStillAFinding": "a refusal caused by the operator's uplink is not evidence about the institution. Adjudicating it as an acquisition failure and spending the next frozen reserve on the same slot would consume a finite, non-renewable resource against a condition that would refuse ANY IPv4-only host from here",
